package app.rwun;

import android.app.Activity;
import android.os.Bundle;
import android.widget.*;

/** Public permission rationale required by the platform Health Connect controller. */
public final class HealthPrivacyActivity extends Activity {
  @Override public void onCreate(Bundle state){
    super.onCreate(state); UiKit.Palette p=new UiKit.Palette(true);
    LinearLayout body=new LinearLayout(this);body.setOrientation(LinearLayout.VERTICAL);int pad=UiKit.dp(this,24);body.setPadding(pad,pad*2,pad,pad);body.setBackgroundColor(p.background);
    body.addView(UiKit.label(this,"OpenRun · Health data",26,p.ink,true));
    body.addView(UiKit.label(this,"Health Connect has independent Read and Write switches. Read data choices include exercise sessions and distance, heart rate, steps, active calories, sleep session windows and resting heart rate. Only selected, permitted data can be read. Daily summaries are displayed on demand and not saved as workouts. Missing readings stay unavailable. Turning Read off pauses Health Connect reads in OpenRun without deleting saved data; system permissions can be revoked in Health Connect. Turning Write off blocks future exports, though an already submitted write may finish. OpenRun reads exercise sessions and distance only after you grant access. Import runs and walks from the last 30 days using Read selected data now. Optional background imports require a separate permission. The separately opted-in Movement & recovery feature can read steps, sleep session windows and resting heart rate after you grant each permission. Sleep and resting heart-rate context is read on demand, not saved. OpenRun does not read medical records or routes through Health Connect. Average heart rate for newly imported runs and walks is read only if you separately grant that permission. OpenRun never deletes Health Connect records. If you separately grant write access and choose and review an original outdoor or indoor run/walk, OpenRun can write its exercise session and known distance. OpenRun does not write imported activities back. The written session uses recorded start/end timestamps, including pauses; active time and distance provenance are included in its notes. Time-only recordings create no distance record. Routes, steps, heart-rate samples and training feedback are not exported. Repeated exports use stable IDs and increasing versions for corrections. Export identity state stays on this phone and is excluded from portable backups; deleting local history does not delete Health Connect records.\n\nImported data stays in private app storage. You can delete saved runs in Progress (most recent deletion can be undone for 15 minutes), remove walking/time-only entries in Indoor progress, or uninstall OpenRun to remove local data. Revoking access in Health Connect stops future reads; it does not delete prior imports. Exported backups contain your saved activity data.\n\nLegacy activity data from earlier releases is retained for backup/export, without active gym or cycling features. Optional local usage counts are off by default, exclude routes and health samples, are never automatically uploaded, and are omitted from backups. Turning them off in Android & privacy erases them. Beta reports and activity cards are shared only through your chosen sharing app after review.\n\nOutdoor walks store GPS time, distance and optional heart rate separately from running. Imported walks are labelled by source. Indoor sessions store time, optional phone step counts, calibration, distance provenance and self-reported feedback locally. Physical activity permission is requested only if you enable phone steps. The step sensor is used only for your active indoor session; no background sitting detection is performed. A health foreground notification accompanies step tracking. Legacy movement and workout reminders are opt-in local notifications with quiet hours, snooze and skip. The optional Movement & recovery feature checks Health Connect step totals during configurable working hours after at least one hour, with a configurable walking break of at least three minutes. Missing or stale steps suppress alerts; low recorded movement does not establish sitting. No background GPS or continuous sensor service is started for this feature. Optional recovery check-ins include sleep, fatigue, soreness, illness, alcohol and pain. Only the latest check-in is retained in separate private storage, expires after seven days and is purged on next app/feature access. All feature state stays outside portable/cloud backups, activity exports, analytics and AI prompts. This feature sends no network requests or model-training input and collects no venue history. Delete its check-in or all feature data in Movement & recovery. Suggestions cannot silently edit a plan or clear a hold. Backup restore leaves reminder consent off and excludes active timers and deletion undo records.\n\nOptional race catalogue refresh contacts your configured HTTPS service; selected event details are stored in training backups. An optional AI explanation sends only the numeric running/plan summary shown in its consent dialog through your configured server to Gemini. No routes, names, heart-rate samples or individual activities are included in that request. AI text cannot change the plan. Server/provider processing terms apply.\n\nOffline Coach uses an optional Gemma model imported or downloaded separately from its publisher. The file is checked against a pinned checksum, stored privately and excluded from backups. Generating an insight processes only the displayed running/plan summary on this phone in a separate app process. It sends no inference request or prompt to a server. Opening the model publisher or choosing a model download requires internet access and is subject to publisher terms. You can remove the weights in Offline Coach. Model explanations cannot edit your schedule or clear a training hold.\n\nThere is no advertising. Optional account/cloud backups use your chosen HTTPS service and encrypt the backup on your phone. Strava activity import/upload uses your configured service only after authorization. Different publishing apps or a separate file import may contain the same activity; review your history for duplicates.",16,p.ink,false));
    body.addView(UiKit.action(this,p,"Back",this::finish));ScrollView scroll=new ScrollView(this);scroll.addView(body);scroll.setOnApplyWindowInsetsListener((v,insets)->{v.setPadding(insets.getSystemWindowInsetLeft(),insets.getSystemWindowInsetTop(),insets.getSystemWindowInsetRight(),insets.getSystemWindowInsetBottom());return insets.consumeSystemWindowInsets();});setContentView(scroll);
  }
}
